From 7b97f0f88dbb734e37c3cc16c43c78a17a50384e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 15:04:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: keep the skip count across the best-equipment search

borg_one_step_wearing_best() carries out, one step at a time, the
equipment changes planned at home by borg_best_stuff().  When the next
change cannot be made because the pack or the home is full, it calls
itself with skip + 1 to try the following change instead.

The skip counter was declared inside the search loop, so it was reset to
skip on every pass and never reached zero: with skip > 0 every remaining
planned change was skipped, not just the first skip of them.  The step
then did nothing, and when the list ended on empty entries the plan was
discarded.  A change that could still be made (for example wearing a
cloak into an empty slot, which also frees the pack slot the blocked
change needs) was never tried.

Declare the counter once, before the loop.

Tracked as diegoami/neo-angband-tracker#85.

(cherry picked from commit 5d73e0c2120b450428f2417db325041c1b6d3da9)
---
 src/borg/borg-item-wear.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-item-wear.c b/src/borg/borg-item-wear.c
index eae1da2b0..dfa4550d7 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-item-wear.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-item-wear.c
@@ -1084,10 +1084,11 @@ static bool borg_one_step_wearing_best(int skip)
     if (!borg.goal.best_item)
         return false;
 
+    /* skip some if there are issues with full inventory */
+    int skipping = skip;
+
     /* find a change */
     while (true) {
-        /* skip some if there are issues with full inventory */
-        int skipping = skip;
         if (borg.goal.best_item[item_num].tval
             || borg.goal.best_item[item_num].pval
             || borg.goal.best_item[item_num].sval) {
